* Circuit 1.2 (procedure part 1) - hysteresis curve, VDD = 10 V. Booklet figure 1.2.
* MC14093 NAND with both inputs tied = Schmitt inverter; thresholds from the datasheet (typ):
* Vp = 5.9 V, Vn = 3.9 V  ->  switch Vt = 4.9, Vh = 1.
* Vin: 5 kHz sine, DC offset 5 V, amplitude 5 V (stays inside 0..VDD), starts at mid-level (start phase does not affect the loop).
* XY plot: V(in) on X, V(out) on Y. Alternative inputs below (comment/uncomment one VIN line).
* Pull-up 1 ohm + switch Ron 1 mohm: charge path = R + 1 ohm and low level ~10 mV, so the
* model adds < 0.1% to the timing (a 100 ohm pull-up had biased f by ~1.6%).
.title Circuit 1.2 hysteresis VDD=10V
VDD  vdd 0   DC 10
VIN  in  0   SIN(5 5 5k)
* VIN in 0 PULSE(0 10 0 100u 100u 0 200u)      ; triangle 5 kHz
* VIN in 0 PULSE(0 10 0 10n 10n 100u 200u)     ; square 5 kHz
RPU  vdd out 1
S1   out 0   in 0   SWS
.model SWS SW(Ron=1m Roff=1e9 Vt=4.9 Vh=1)
.tran 0.2u 0.6m
.end
